PATCH 541: the weapon-station service cluster -- six functions that host-deref'd the object near
offset, and two dropped carries that made a whole branch dead code.

Found by driving combat hard enough to reach it: with board:0018's LOS probe forcing target
acquisition to succeed, AZER1 SIGSEGVs inside FUN_0000_86e3 (measured param_1=0xC157, a DGROUP near
offset used as a host pointer) on the path afa2 -> 8711 -> 86e3.

  86e3  asm 0x86e3-0x8710.  Picks station 0 if `[di+0xb7]==4 && [di+0xb5]!=0`, else station 1 if
        `[di+0xb8]==4`, else `86fe stc` and returns.  On success calls 0f69:0x8be0 (linear 0x18270 =
        FUN_1000_8270 -- the port's target was already right), sets [di+0xe0]/[di+0xe2]=3, `870f clc`.
        Ghidra host-deref'd the object AND dropped the carry.
  8711  asm 0x8711-0x8719 is `call 86e3 ; jae 8719 ; call 86b8`.  So 86b8 runs exactly when 86e3
        returned CARRY SET.  Ghidra emitted `undefined1 in_CF = 0;` -- a fabricated local -- making
        FUN_0000_86b8 unreachable dead code.
  86b8  asm 0x86b8-0x86de.  Claims the first free station slot (`[di+bx+0xb7]==0` -> set 2), `86cc stc`
        when neither is free, `86dd clc` when one was claimed.  Same base-loss, same dropped carry.
  8270  asm 0x18270-0x182b5 (= 0f69:0x8be0), the FIRE service.  Host-deref'd the firer AND the target
        link: `18277 mov 0x97(%di),%si ; 1827f testb $0x10,0x16(%si)` reads the TARGET's flags through
        SI, a DGROUP near offset, which the pristine code dereferenced as a host pointer.  It also
        bound b1df's new object to a dead `unaff_CS` and its carry to a dead `bVar4`, discarding the
        spawn result -- the asm's `1828e call b1df ; 18291 mov %di,%si ; 18293 pop %di` puts the NEW
        object in SI and restores the firer in DI (the patch-462 split).
  842f  asm 0x842f-0x844a.  `8436 mov -0x6f9e(%bx),%bx` reads word[DGROUP:bx*2+0x9062], a per-station
        field offset, which Ghidra deref'd as a host int*; `843f pop %bx` restores the UNSHIFTED
        station index for the 8be0 call.
  844b  asm 0x844b, one line: `xorb $0x8,0x3f(%di)`, host-deref'd.

Callee conventions are unchanged and each call site matched to what its callee already expects:
b8d1 takes HOST pointers, c047 and a4a2 take NEAR OFFSETS, b1df returns the new object's near offset.

Default build: AZER1/AZER4/SAUDI2/TRAIN1 outcomes unchanged (no regression) -- this path is rarely
reached today precisely because board:0018's LOS stand-in stops units from acquiring targets.
Under the LOS probe the 86e3 SIGSEGV is gone; AZER1 then reaches FUN_0000_9f66, which board:0019
already names as the next open entry of the same class.

